ONEDRAFT
CAD-AI — Aria Powered
Identity, Access Control & Security System
Version 1.0
Status: Implementation Specification
Security Model: Multi-Tenant RBAC + Capability Authorization
Authentication: Bearer Token / OIDC-Compatible
Authorization: Organization / Project / Resource Scope
Identifiers: UUID
Primary Security Boundary: Organization → Project → Resource
AI Security Boundary: Aria → Application Capabilities → Domain Services

1. SECURITY DESIGN PRINCIPLE
Security is a foundational subsystem of OneDraft rather than an external feature added after implementation.
Every operation entering the platform must establish:
Who is making the request
What organization they belong to
What project they are accessing
What resource they are attempting to access
What operation they are attempting to perform
Whether the operation is authorized
Whether the operation is permitted in the current project state
The security system therefore operates before domain mutation, document generation, geometry execution, compliance execution, artifact access, and Aria command execution.
The security architecture becomes:
IDENTITY
    ↓
AUTHENTICATION
    ↓
ORGANIZATION MEMBERSHIP
    ↓
PROJECT AUTHORIZATION
    ↓
RESOURCE AUTHORIZATION
    ↓
CAPABILITY AUTHORIZATION
    ↓
DOMAIN OPERATION
    ↓
AUDIT EVENT

2. SECURITY DOMAINS
The OneDraft security subsystem shall initially contain:
identity
authorization
security
audit
system
The existing:
identity.users
identity.organizations
identity.organization_members
remain the authoritative identity records.
The security subsystem extends those records without redefining the underlying identity architecture.

3. SECURITY PRINCIPLES
OneDraft shall implement:
Least privilege
Explicit authorization
Project isolation
Organization isolation
Deny by default
Capability-based execution
Immutable security events
Credential separation
Service identity separation
Short-lived access tokens
Auditable privileged operations
No direct database access by external clients

4. AUTHENTICATION BOUNDARY
External clients authenticate against the OneDraft authentication boundary.
The architecture is:
CLIENT
 ↓
AUTHENTICATION PROVIDER
 ↓
ACCESS TOKEN
 ↓
API GATEWAY
 ↓
AUTHORIZATION
 ↓
DOMAIN SERVICES
The domain services do not independently implement separate user authentication systems.
Authentication establishes identity.
Authorization establishes permission.
These concerns must remain separate.

5. USER IDENTITY
The authoritative user record remains:
identity.users
The security layer associates authenticated identities with:
user_id
organization_id
membership
roles
scopes
session
authentication_events
No service may create an independent user identity for normal application access.

6. SERVICE IDENTITIES
Internal services shall have independent identities.
Examples:
api-service
runtime-orchestrator
geometry-worker
compliance-worker
validation-worker
documentation-worker
artifact-service
event-bus
aria-orchestrator
notification-service
A service identity is distinct from a human user.
Service actions therefore record:
actor_type = SERVICE
actor_id = service_identity_id
Human actions record:
actor_type = USER
actor_id = user_id

