15. RESOURCE AUTHORIZATION
Authorization must occur at multiple levels.
ORGANIZATION
    ↓
PROJECT
    ↓
RESOURCE
    ↓
OPERATION
For example:
A user may have permission to:
project:read
without having permission to:
aria:execute
Likewise, a user may have:
aria:execute
within Project A while having no authorization against Project B.

16. PROJECT TENANCY ISOLATION
Every project operation must resolve:
organization_id
project_id
actor_id
before accessing project data.
The system must prevent cross-organization resource access even where a valid UUID is supplied.
A valid object identifier does not constitute authorization.
The authorization boundary must verify ownership through the project hierarchy.

17. RESOURCE OWNERSHIP
Resource ownership is derived wherever possible.
Example:
drawing
 ↓
project
 ↓
organization
Therefore:
drawing.project_id
determines the authorization boundary.
The system must not trust a client-supplied:
organization_id
as proof of ownership.

18. CAPABILITY AUTHORIZATION
High-impact operations shall use explicit capabilities.
Examples:
CREATE_PROJECT
MODIFY_MODEL
EXECUTE_ARIA_COMMAND
EXECUTE_GEOMETRY
EXECUTE_COMPLIANCE
EXECUTE_VALIDATION
GENERATE_DRAWING
GENERATE_DOCUMENT
RESOLVE_REDLINE
ACCEPT_DOCUMENT_PACKAGE
A capability is granted only after the authorization service confirms the actor's permissions.

