43. ADMINISTRATIVE OPERATIONS
Administrative actions must be explicitly identified.
Examples:
organization administration
membership administration
role administration
security policy administration
billing administration
project ownership transfer
Administrative actions receive enhanced audit records.

44. BREAK-GLASS ACCESS
A future controlled emergency-access mechanism may exist for system operators.
Any such access must require:
explicit activation
reason
operator identity
time limit
scope
complete audit trail
Break-glass access must never become a permanent authorization path.

45. FINALIZED PROJECT SECURITY
A finalized document package requires stronger controls.
Once finalized:
PROJECT
 ↓
FINAL REVISION
 ↓
VALIDATION
 ↓
DOCUMENT PACKAGE
 ↓
ACCEPTANCE
Subsequent modifications create a new revision rather than silently modifying the finalized state.
Authorization therefore works together with revision control.

46. SECURITY AND REVISION INTEGRATION
A command must verify both:
AUTHORIZATION
and:
EXPECTED_REVISION
Example:
authorized user
+
expected_revision = 17
+
current_revision = 17
permits execution.
If:
expected_revision = 17
current_revision = 18
the command is rejected as stale regardless of authorization.

47. SECURITY AND COMPLIANCE INTEGRATION
Authorization does not override regulatory validation.
The command path remains:
AUTHORIZATION
 ↓
MODEL COMMAND
 ↓
CONSTRAINT CHECK
 ↓
COMPLIANCE / VALIDATION
 ↓
COMMIT
A user authorized to make a design change does not automatically authorize the system to accept an invalid design state.

48. SECURITY AND REDLINES
Redline creation and redline resolution are separately authorized operations.
For example:
redline:create
does not necessarily grant:
redline:resolve
Likewise:
redline:resolve
does not permit bypassing model validation.

49. SECURITY AND DOCUMENT GENERATION
Document generation requires:
project access
+
document generation permission
+
valid revision
+
required validation state
The document engine must reject unauthorized or invalid generation requests.

50. SECURITY AND CUSTOMER ACCEPTANCE
Acceptance is a controlled operation.
The acceptance workflow verifies:
customer identity
project authorization
revision identity
model version
document package
validation state
The acceptance record then becomes immutable except through an explicit superseding workflow.

51. API SECURITY ENDPOINTS
The initial API security surface shall include:
GET /api/v1/me
GET /api/v1/me/organizations
GET /api/v1/me/projects
GET /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/members
POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/members
