65. CONTENT INTEGRITY
Generated artifacts should retain:
content_hash
The hash becomes part of document provenance.
For final packages:
PROJECT
 ↓
REVISION
 ↓
MODEL VERSION
 ↓
CODE MANIFEST
 ↓
VALIDATION
 ↓
DOCUMENT PACKAGE
 ↓
CONTENT HASH
Security and provenance therefore remain connected.

66. SECURITY TESTING
The initial security test suite shall verify:
unauthenticated access rejected

invalid token rejected

expired token rejected

revoked token rejected

cross-organization access rejected

cross-project access rejected

insufficient role rejected

insufficient scope rejected

unauthorized Aria command rejected

stale revision rejected

unauthorized artifact access rejected

unauthorized document generation rejected

unauthorized acceptance rejected

worker impersonation rejected

event replay without authorization rejected

67. TENANT ISOLATION TEST
A mandatory integration test shall attempt:
Organization A
 ↓
Project A
to access:
Organization B
 ↓
Project B
using valid authentication credentials belonging to Organization A.
The request must fail.
No project object, document, geometry, event, or artifact from Project B may be disclosed.

68. ARIA SECURITY TEST
The test shall submit an Aria command requesting an operation for which the authenticated actor lacks authorization.
Expected result:
AUTHORIZATION_DENIED
No:
model mutation
revision
geometry job
drawing job
document
may be created.
The denial itself is audited.

69. PRIVILEGED COMMAND TEST
The test shall submit a privileged command without the required approval.
Expected result:
REQUIRES_APPROVAL
The system must not execute the command.

70. SECURITY REGRESSION TEST
Every future subsystem must preserve:
authentication
authorization
tenant isolation
project isolation
resource ownership
revision integrity
artifact protection
auditability
Security therefore becomes a cross-cutting regression requirement for all future OneDraft services.

